    "body": "A late-evening slot shows up on the wrong calendar day.\n\n**Repro**\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom scheduler.booking import daily_agenda\n\nslots = [datetime(2026, 3, 16, 2, 0, tzinfo=timezone.utc)]\nprint(daily_agenda(slots, \"America/Mexico_City\"))\n```\n\n**Observed:** `{\"2026-03-16\": [\"20:00\"]}`\n**Expected:** `{\"2026-03-15\": [\"20:00\"]}`\n\n02:00 UTC on the 16th is 20:00 on the 15th in Mexico City. The displayed time\nis right; the day it is grouped under is wrong, so the slot lands in the wrong\ncalendar cell.\n\nThe current tests pass — none of them covers `daily_agenda`.",
